WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.142
Create a regular user with a name and sign-in password.

2
00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:06.418
Select the user role.

3
00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:11.050
Use a regular account when configuring model access restrictions.

4
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:16.480
Open the user’s cost budgets and add a monthly budget of ten dollars.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.025
Costs use your configured model prices and are separate from the
upstream account balance.

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.955
Add an allow rule for demo-user and set the model pattern to demo-*.

7
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:31.292
This user can access matching model routes.

8
00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:34.475
Other models remain denied by default.

9
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.755
Create a client key for this user and give it a recognizable name.

10
00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:42.542
Keep management access disabled.

11
00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:46.938
Without an additional key budget, the user’s budget still applies.

12
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.392
Copy the key immediately and save it in the client.

13
00:00:51.412 --> 00:00:58.088
Secret retention is disabled here, so the complete value cannot be
revealed again after closing this dialog.

14
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.668
The new key can call demo-chat and receive a reply.

15
00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:09.538
A model outside the allowed pattern returns HTTP 403, confirming that
the permission rule is active.
